comments.body:
@yaronf, there could be unknown to the peer number of relevant identities.

For example, a VDI farm client connecting to a server may want to signal certificates associated with all the logged on users. The server does not know how many users there are, so it does not know how many `certificate_request_context` to generate. `max_certificates` allows the flexibility and also offers a way to signal a limit.

I'm happy to keep this issue open for now.

`supplemental_certificate_requests` signals support for the mechanism and optionally provides request context similarly to `CertificateRequest` and relevant extensions in `ClientHello`. `supplemental_certificate` flag indicates that at least one additional supplemental certificate flight comes after the corresponding `Certificate`/`CertificateVerify`/`Finished`.
`supplemental_certificate` flag and the supplemental certificate flights must not be included if the peer did not include `supplemental_certificate_requests` extension previously.

@yaronf, do you think this needs to be spelled out better in the draft text?

```suggestion
  Extension extensions<2..2^16-1>;
```
